The Hidden Boss's room, the summoning's light: a second go at it (Eric, Nov 13, of the mockup's first: "the light doesn't look
right ... it's close, but maybe you could try, take a shot at it"). For the room's own branch to take or leave; nothing here is in
the game.

Applies to branch claude/hidden-boss-room at 73f64556 (one file, the light's section at its end; the beats and their times are
untouched):   git apply scripts/reel/patches/hidden-room-summoning-light.patch
Seen on the dev server at /hidden-room-preview.html?ui=0 (the Summon button, or ?summon=<ms>).

What changed: the board is the lamp. Its face blazes; a shaft of light stands on it; rays rise from its face up and outward, each a
line in the room through the room's own camera (proj), soft-edged, coming up out of nothing at its foot and gone at its tip; more
rays lie along the floor, flattened as the floor is; a pool of light spreads on the boards round it; and the room dims while the
light is on, so it reads as light. The splash's rings and drops are on the floor through the camera too. Five small sprites made
once and stretched: no gradient is built in a frame. About 45 draws a frame while the light is on; frame rate not measured.
Checked: typecheck, packages/app/test/recluse-room.test.ts, and frames on a computer (960 x 600) and a phone (390 x 760).

